  "summary": "Okafor CRC 2026 worklist (RBC-QM-02), 4 members:\n\n| Patient | Status | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| pt-0009 Elly Trantow (72) | Open gap: FIT kit ordered (sr-t0005), outreach sent (comm-t0006) | No qualifying screening on record. She first looked excluded (active Frailty plus donepezil), but Dr. Lin's message of 10/23 (comm-00301) says the Frailty entry cond-00189 was put on her chart in error, and it is now marked entered in error. That removes the exclusion. No nursing home, hospice/palliative care, CRC or colectomy. |\n| pt-0020 Kelsie Rohan (52) | Excluded | Hospice episode eoc-00002 (finished) ran 06/16 to 08/21/2026, in the measurement period. The outside discharge summary doc-00402 confirms it (she revoked hospice to join a trial). No order, no contact. |\n| pt-0022 Tiny Koss (52) | Open gap: FIT kit ordered (sr-t0001), outreach sent (comm-t0003) | A corrected result for FIT obs-01732 moved the collection date to 12/31/2025 (01/05/2026 was when the lab received it). That puts it outside 2026, so it doesn't count. No other qualifying test and no exclusions. |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver (51) | Open gap: FIT kit ordered (sr-t0002), outreach sent (comm-t0004) | The lab withdrew the 06/11/2024 sDNA-FIT (obs-01871): it was another patient's specimen and is now marked entered in error (doc-00401). The 2025 colonoscopy referral sr-00003 is still active but was never done, and a referral doesn't count as screening. No exclusions. |\n\nEach FIT order's window is 2026-10-23 to 2026-12-31. No member had an active FIT order before this. The outreach messages say the kit is coming and how to collect and return it; they make no claims about past screening. I wrote a decision note in each member's chart (doc-t0007 to doc-t0010) citing RBC-QM-02.\n\nFour items arrived after I started (inbox-a0001 to a0004), all about these patients, and I reviewed and completed each one:\n- Lin message (a0001): reversed my earlier exclusion of pt-0009 before I had recorded it, 